  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.3.0 - The manual that ships with this repository is now generated by the library it documents: tools/SharpCorePDF.Manual prints the book headlessly and finishes it with SharpCorePDF's own reader, authoring surface and edit plan, so the running footer, the outline and the metadata are one plan and neither Python nor pypdf takes part. Fixes three faults a reader could see: a layer drawn under a graphics state the page leaves open (Chromium's print output states its transform outside a q, which put the manual's footer at a quarter of its size in the top-left corner), a footer anchor measured from the wrong edge, and a Quickstart that promised a container package it did not reference. Both legs (net10.0, net11.0) ship in one package. Details: https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SharpCorePDF/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
